<h2 id=3D"grid-editor" data-text=3D"CSS grid editor" tabindex=3D"-1">CSS gr=
id editor</h2>

<p>A highly requested feature. You can now preview and author CSS Grid with=
 the new CSS Grid editor!</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/css-grid-editor-d75e8f3fa924d.png" alt=3D"CSS Grid editor" width=3D"8=
00" height=3D"486"></p>

<p>When an HTML element on your page has <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr"=
>display: grid</code> or <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">display: inline=
-grid</code> applied to it, you can see an icon appear next to it in the St=
yles pane. Click the icon to toggle the CSS grid editor. Here you can previ=
ew the potential changes with the on screen icons (e.g. <code translate=3D"=
no" dir=3D"ltr">justify-content: space-around</code>) and author the grid a=
ppearance with just one click.</p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1203241">1203241</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"const-redeclaration" data-text=3D"Support for const redeclaration=
s in the Console" tabindex=3D"-1">Support for <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D=
"ltr">const</code> redeclarations in the Console</h2>

<p>The Console now supports redeclaration of <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"=
ltr">const</code> statement, in addition to the existing <a href=3D"https:/=
/developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-devtools-80#redeclarations"><code transla=
te=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">let</code> and <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">cla=
ss</code> redeclarations</a>. The inability to redeclare was a common annoy=
ance for web developers who use the Console to experiment with new JavaScri=
pt code.</p>

<p>This allows developers to copy-paste code into the DevTools console to s=
ee how it works or experiment, make small changes to the code, and repeat t=
he process without refreshing the page. Previously, DevTools threw a syntax=
 error if the code redeclared a <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">const</c=
ode> binding.</p>

<p>Refer to the example below. <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">const</co=
de> redeclaration is supported <strong>across separate REPL scripts</strong=
> (refer to variable <code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">a</code>). Take not=
e that the following scenarios are not supported by design:</p>

<ul>
<li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">const</code> redeclaration of page s=
cripts is not allowed in REPL scripts</li>
<li><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">const</code> redeclaration within th=
e same REPL script is not allowed (refer to variable <code translate=3D"no"=
 dir=3D"ltr">b</code>)</li>
</ul>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/const-redeclarations-7e0aa5c62ea58.png" alt=3D"const redeclarations" =
width=3D"800" height=3D"496"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1076427">1076427</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"source-order" data-text=3D"Source order viewer" tabindex=3D"-1">S=
ource order viewer</h2>

<p>You can now view the order of source elements on screen for better acces=
sibility inspection.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/source-order-viewer-e61210f86bccd.png" alt=3D"Source order viewer" wi=
dth=3D"800" height=3D"515"></p>

<p>The order of content in an HTML document is important for search engine =
optimization and accessibility. The newer CSS features allow developers to =
create content that looks very different in its on-screen order than what i=
s in the HTML document. This is a big accessibility problem as screen reade=
r users would get a different, most likely confusing experience than sighte=
d users.</p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1094406">1094406</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"frame-details" data-text=3D"New shortcut to view frame details" t=
abindex=3D"-1">New shortcut to view frame details</h2>

<p>View iframe details by right-clicking on the iframe element in the Eleme=
nts panel, and select <strong>Show frame details</strong>.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/show-frame-details-b74482e0589ec.png" alt=3D"Show frame details" widt=
h=3D"800" height=3D"486"></p>

<p>This takes you to a view of the iframe's details in the Application pane=
l where you can examine document details, security &amp; isolation status, =
<a href=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/privacy-sandbox/permissions-po=
licy">permissions policy</a>, and more to debug potential issues.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/frame-details-view-27c89f4a83ad1.png" alt=3D"Frame details view" widt=
h=3D"800" height=3D"516"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1192084">1192084</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"cors" data-text=3D"Enhanced CORS debugging support" tabindex=3D"-=
1">Enhanced CORS debugging support</h2>

<p>Cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) errors are now surfaced in the Issu=
es tab. There are various reasons causing CORS errors. Click to expand each=
 issue to understand the potential causes and solutions.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/cors-issues-the-issues-t-309a0d2a5a818.png" alt=3D"CORS issues in the=
 Issues tab" width=3D"800" height=3D"490"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1141824">1141824</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"network" data-text=3D"Network panel updates" tabindex=3D"-1">Netw=
ork panel updates</h2>

<h3 id=3D"fetch-xhr" data-text=3D"Rename XHR label to Fetch/XHR" tabindex=
=3D"-1">Rename XHR label to Fetch/<wbr>XHR</h3>

<p>The XHR label is now renamed to <strong>Fetch/XHR</strong>. This change =
makes it clearer that this filter includes both <a href=3D"https://xhr.spec=
.whatwg.org/"><code translate=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">XMLHttpRequest</code></a> =
and <a href=3D"https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/">Fetch API</a> network reques=
ts.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/fetchxhr-label-96ad5f9ca594d.png" alt=3D"Fetch/XHR label" width=3D"80=
0" height=3D"516"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1201398">1201398</a></p>

<h3 id=3D"wasm" data-text=3D"Filter Wasm resource type in the Network panel=
" tabindex=3D"-1">Filter Wasm resource type in the Network panel</h3>

<p>You can now click on the new <strong>Wasm</strong> button to filter the =
Wasm network requests.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/filter-wasm-18f30b5cc1e7c.png" alt=3D"Filter by Wasm" width=3D"800" h=
eight=3D"515"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1103638">1103638</a></p>

<h3 id=3D"sec-ua-ch" data-text=3D"User-Agent Client Hints for devices in th=
e Network conditions tab" tabindex=3D"-1">User-Agent Client Hints for devic=
es in the Network conditions tab</h3>

<p><a href=3D"https://web.dev/user-agent-client-hints">User-Agent Client Hi=
nts</a> are now applied for devices in the <strong>User agent</strong> fiel=
d under <strong>Network conditions</strong> tab.</p>

<p>User-Agent Client Hints are a new expansion to the Client Hints API, tha=
t enables developers to access information about a user's browser in a priv=
acy-preserving and ergonomic way.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/user-agent-client-hints-88da6b974aa53.png" alt=3D"User-Agent Client H=
ints for devices in the Network conditions tab" width=3D"800" height=3D"532=
"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1174299">1174299</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"quirks-mode" data-text=3D"Report Quirks mode issues in the Issues=
 tab" tabindex=3D"-1">Report Quirks mode issues in the Issues tab</h2>

<p>DevTools now reports <a href=3D"https://quirks.spec.whatwg.org/">Quirks =
Mode</a> and <a href=3D"https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-limit=
ed-quirks">Limited-quirks Mode</a> issues.</p>

<p>Quirks Mode and Limited-quirks Mode are legacy browser modes from before=
 the web standards were made. These modes emulate pre-standard-era layout b=
ehaviors that often cause unexpected visual effects.</p>

<p>When debugging layout issues, developers might think they are caused by =
user-authored CSS or HTML bugs, while the real problem is the Compat Mode t=
he page is in. DevTools provides suggestions for fixing it.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/report-quirks-mode-issues-aba7e5f7a0ccc.png" alt=3D"Report Quirks mod=
e issues in the Issues tab" width=3D"800" height=3D"490"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/622660">622660</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"computed-intersections" data-text=3D"Include Compute Intersection=
s in the Performance panel" tabindex=3D"-1">Include Compute Intersections i=
n the Performance panel</h2>

<p>DevTools now show the <strong>Compute Intersections</strong> in the flam=
e chart. These changes help you to identify the <a href=3D"https://web.dev/=
articles/intersectionobserver-v2">intersection observers</a> events and deb=
ug on its potential performance overheads.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/compute-intersections-th-26bbee4a53932.png" alt=3D"Compute Intersecti=
ons in the Performance panel" width=3D"800" height=3D"496"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1199137">1199137</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"lighthouse" data-text=3D"Lighthouse 7.5 in the Lighthouse panel" =
tabindex=3D"-1">Lighthouse 7.<wbr>5 in the Lighthouse panel</h2>

<p>The Lighthouse panel is now running Lighthouse 7.5. The "missing explici=
t width and height" warning is now removed for images with <code translate=
=3D"no" dir=3D"ltr">aspect-ratio</code> defined in CSS. Previously, Lightho=
use showed warnings for images without width and height defined.</p>

<p>Check out the <a href=3D"https://github.com/GoogleChrome/lighthouse/rele=
ases/tag/v7.5.0">release notes</a> for a full list of changes.</p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/772558">772558</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"restart-frame" data-text=3D"Deprecated &quot;Restart frame&quot; =
context menu in the call stack" tabindex=3D"-1">Deprecated "Restart frame" =
context menu in the call stack</h2>

<p>The <strong>Restart frame</strong> option is now deprecated. This featur=
e requires further development to work well, it is currently broken and oft=
en crashes.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/deprecated-restart-frame-eb3d09a3320a7.png" alt=3D"Deprecated Restart=
 frame context menu" width=3D"800" height=3D"486"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1203606">1203606</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"protocol-monitor" data-text=3D"[Experimental] Protocol monitor" t=
abindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" role=
=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"2">[Experimental] Protocol monitor</span><button=
 type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-icons" =
aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: [Experimental] Protocol monitor" d=
ata-title=3D"Copy link to this section: [Experimental] Protocol monitor" da=
ta-id=3D"protocol-monitor"></button></h2>

<aside class=3D"note"><b>Note:</b> To enable the experiment, check the <str=
ong>Protocol Monitor</strong> checkbox under <strong>Settings</strong> &gt;=
 <strong>Experiments</strong>.</aside>

<p>Chrome DevTools uses the <a href=3D"https://chromedevtools.github.io/dev=
tools-protocol/">Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)</a> to instrument, inspect,=
 debug and profile Chrome browsers. The <strong>Protocol monitor</strong> p=
rovides you a way to view all the CDP requests and responses made by DevToo=
ls.</p>

<p>Two new functions added to facilitate the testing of CDP:</p>

<ul>
<li>The new <strong>Save</strong> button allows you to download the recorde=
d messages as a JSON file</li>
<li>A new field that allows you to send a raw CDP command directly</li>
</ul>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/protocol-monitor-7f93a41fef823.png" alt=3D"Protocol monitor" width=3D=
"800" height=3D"496"></p>

<p>Chromium issues: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1204004">1204004</a>, <a h=
ref=3D"https://crbug.com/1204466">1204466</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"puppeteer-recorder" data-text=3D"[Experimental] Puppeteer Recorde=
r" tabindex=3D"-1" role=3D"presentation"><span class=3D"devsite-heading" ro=
le=3D"heading" aria-level=3D"2">[Experimental] Puppeteer Recorder</span><bu=
tton type=3D"button" class=3D"devsite-heading-link button-flat material-ico=
ns" aria-label=3D"Copy link to this section: [Experimental] Puppeteer Recor=
der" data-title=3D"Copy link to this section: [Experimental] Puppeteer Reco=
rder" data-id=3D"puppeteer-recorder"></button></h2>

<aside class=3D"note"><b>Note:</b> To enable the experiment, check the <str=
ong>Recorder</strong> checkbox under <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong=
>Experiments</strong>.</aside>

<p>The <a href=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-devtools-89#reco=
rd">Puppeteer recorder</a> now generates a list of steps based on your inte=
raction with the browser, whereas previously DevTools generated a Puppeteer=
 script directly instead. A new <strong>Export</strong> button is added to =
allow you export the steps as a Puppeteer script.</p>

<p>After recording the steps, you can use the new <strong>Replay</strong> b=
utton to replay the steps. Follow the <a href=3D"https://developer.chrome.c=
om/blog/new-in-devtools-89#record">instructions here</a> to learn how to ge=
t started with recording.</p>

<p>Please note that this is an early-stage experiment. We plan to improve a=
nd expand the Recorder functionality over time.</p>

<p><img src=3D"https://developer.chrome.com/static/blog/new-in-devtools-92/=
image/puppeteer-recorder-0faa983b0df33.png" alt=3D"Puppeteer Recorder" widt=
h=3D"800" height=3D"557"></p>

<p>Chromium issue: <a href=3D"https://crbug.com/1199787">1199787</a></p>

<h2 id=3D"preview-channels" data-text=3D"Download the preview channels" tab=
index=3D"-1">Download the preview channels</h2>

<p>Consider using the Chrome <a href=3D"https://www.google.com/chrome/canar=
y/">Canary</a>, <a href=3D"https://www.google.com/chrome/dev/">Dev</a>, or =
<a href=3D"https://www.google.com/chrome/beta/">Beta</a> as your default de=
velopment browser. These preview channels give you access to the latest Dev=
Tools features, let you test cutting-edge web platform APIs, and help you f=
ind issues on your site before your users do!</p>

<h2 id=3D"contact-us" data-text=3D"Get in touch with the Chrome DevTools te=
am" tabindex=3D"-1">Get in touch with the Chrome Dev<wbr>Tools team</h2>

<p>Use the following options to discuss the new features, updates, or anyth=
ing else related to DevTools.</p>

<ul>
<li>Submit feedback and feature requests to us at <a href=3D"https://crbug.=
com/">crbug.com</a>.</li>
<li>Report a DevTools issue using the <span class=3D"material-symbols-outli=
ned" aria-hidden=3D"true">more_vert</span> <strong>More options</strong> &g=
t; <strong>Help</strong> &gt; <strong>Report a DevTools issue</strong> in D=
evTools.</li>
<li>Tweet at <a href=3D"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=3D@ChromeDevT=
ools" target=3D"_blank">@ChromeDevTools</a>.</li>
<li>Leave comments on <a href=3D"https://goo.gle/devtools-youtube">What's n=
ew in DevTools YouTube videos</a> or <a href=3D"https://goo.gle/devtools-ti=
ps">DevTools Tips YouTube videos</a>.</li>
</ul>

